     "en": "A short story"
    },
    "text": {
     "en": "Raju saw a floor covered with hexagonal tiles with no gaps.\n\"Tiling,\" said his father."
    }
   },
   {
    "id": "explain",
    "type": "explanation",
    "provenance": "original",
    "keepEnglishTerms": [
     "tiling",
     "tessellation",
     "corner"
    ],
    "text": {
     "en": "Tiling means covering a flat surface with shapes without gaps or overlaps. Regular tiles of one kind are possible only for equilateral triangles, squares and regular hexagons.\nThis works because the angles at a corner must add up to 360 degrees. Six triangles of 60 degrees, four squares of 90 degrees and three hexagons of 120 degrees each make 360.\nA regular pentagon has angles of 108 degrees, which do not divide 360, so it cannot tile alone."
    }
   },
